{
  "slug": "nova-thesis",
  "name": "Nova Thesis",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "nova-thesis challenges technical implementations before they ship. Present any implementation — a problem statement, a design sketch, a code snippet, or a full repository — and the skill refuses to accept it at\nface value. It scores the work across five dimensions (Correctness, Completeness, Scalability, Security, Maintainability), surfaces a real-world incident from an index of public postmortems that matches the\nriskiest gap, and asks hard, specific questions anchored to that incident. It keeps pushing until every dimension scores at least 7/10, or until you consciously name and accept the remaining trade-offs.\n\nUnlike review tools that confirm, nova-thesis is built to find where things break — before production does. Read-only, MIT licensed, no telemetry, no external services required. Ships with 20 test scenarios and\na defended-thesis example that proves the skill also correctly approves strong work.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `challenging-implementations` (Use when someone presents a technical, software, or AI/ML implementation — whether a problem, idea, approach, code snippet,…).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install nova-thesis@claude-community` from `jerry7991/nova-thesis`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
